# Token-saving rules

- Never read the entire repository unless explicitly required.
- First identify relevant files.
- Search symbols before opening files.
- Read only the required sections.
- Do not repeat code already available in context.
- Do not reproduce unchanged files.
- Return minimal patches/diffs when possible.
- Reuse existing components and utilities.
- Check existing dependencies before adding packages.
- Check existing environment/configuration before creating new configuration.
- Avoid unnecessary explanations during implementation.
- Do not inspect generated files unless required.
- Ignore `node_modules`, build output, caches, and binaries.
- Prefer repository search over broad file loading.
- For errors, inspect the smallest relevant execution path first.
- Make one logical change at a time.
- Run targeted tests before the full test suite.
- Summarize completed changes instead of repeating source code.
- Keep MCP tool usage focused; do not call every available MCP.
